{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-58548","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113100","text":"R0.4.7 atomic lifecycle admission — written before the mechanism"}]},{"id":"blk-58549","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113101","text":"Invariant from the R0.4.6 review:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58551","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113102","marks":["bold"],"text":"No authority-bearing lifecycle transition may take effect without consuming the current lifecycle admission capability that makes that transition current."}]}],"id":"blk-58550","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-58552","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113103","text":"The hole"}]},{"id":"blk-58553","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113104","text":"<!-- historical --> R0.4.6 serialized "},{"id":"spn-113105","marks":["italic"],"text":"evidence"},{"id":"spn-113106","text":" (linear head, no rollback) but not "},{"id":"spn-113107","marks":["italic"],"text":"operational mutation"},{"id":"spn-113108","text":": capability transitions ("},{"id":"spn-113109","marks":["code"],"text":"attach"},{"id":"spn-113110","text":", "},{"id":"spn-113111","marks":["code"],"text":"detach"},{"id":"spn-113112","text":", "},{"id":"spn-113113","marks":["code"],"text":"finalize_loss"},{"id":"spn-113114","text":", "},{"id":"spn-113115","marks":["code"],"text":"reopen"},{"id":"spn-113116","text":") ran independently, minted a Copy event, and the head was advanced later by a separate "},{"id":"spn-113117","marks":["code"],"text":"append"},{"id":"spn-113118","text":". In the gap the head lagged reality, and three forks followed:"}]},{"id":"blk-58554","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58556","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113119","marks":["code"],"text":"detach()"},{"id":"spn-113120","text":" produced Vacant(1) before its receipt was appended; the"}]}],"id":"blk-58555","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-58557","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113121","text":"warden finalized A@0 against the still-current head; "},{"id":"spn-113122","marks":["code"],"text":"reopen"},{"id":"spn-113123","text":" produced a second Vacant(1). Two carriers attached at generation 1."}]},{"id":"blk-58558","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58560","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113124","text":"Vacant(1) consumed to attach B before B's record was appended; the"}]}],"id":"blk-58559","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-58561","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113125","text":"head still said vacant; "},{"id":"spn-113126","marks":["code"],"text":"reopen"},{"id":"spn-113127","text":" minted another Vacant(1). B and C."}]},{"id":"blk-58562","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58564","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113128","text":"After accepted finality of A@0 and attachment of B@1, the stale"}]}],"id":"blk-58563","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-58565","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113129","marks":["code"],"text":"LocusAttachment(A,0)"},{"id":"spn-113130","text":" value still existed and could "},{"id":"spn-113131","marks":["code"],"text":"detach()"},{"id":"spn-113132","text":" into yet another Vacant(1). Evidence said A was fenced; A was not "},{"id":"spn-113133","marks":["italic"],"text":"operationally"},{"id":"spn-113134","text":" fenced. <!-- /historical -->"}]},{"id":"blk-58566","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113135","text":"Closure: the linear token is admission, and every mutation consumes it"}]},{"id":"blk-58567","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113136","marks":["code"],"text":"LifecycleHead"},{"id":"spn-113137","text":" is renamed "},{"id":"spn-113138","marks":["code"],"text":"LifecycleAdmission"},{"id":"spn-113139","text":": it is no longer knowledge with a linear identity, it is the single serialization point that makes a mutation current. "},{"id":"spn-113140","marks":["code"],"text":"LifecycleState"},{"id":"spn-113141","text":" remains descriptive knowledge."}]},{"id":"blk-58568","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Vacant + Admission ──attach(c)──► Attachment + AttachRecord + Admission'\nAttachment + Admission ──detach()──► Vacant + DetachReceipt + Admission'\nWarden(&) + Admission ──finalize_loss──► LossFinalization + Vacant + Admission'"},{"id":"blk-58569","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58571","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113142","text":"Each transition CONSUMES the admission and returns the successor; the"}]}],"id":"blk-58570","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58572","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113143","text":"evidence record it emits "},{"id":"spn-113144","marks":["italic"],"text":"describes an already-serialized transition"},{"id":"spn-113145","text":" (records stay Copy; they are no longer the later operation that makes a completed mutation current)."}]},{"id":"blk-58573","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58575","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113146","text":"Every failure path returns the un-consumed capability AND the"}]}],"id":"blk-58574","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58576","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113147","text":"un-consumed admission with the error, so a retry cannot mint duplicates and a wrong call never destroys linear state. <!-- historical -->"}]},{"id":"blk-58577","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58579","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113148","text":"The R0.4.6 "},{"id":"spn-113149","marks":["code"],"text":"append"},{"id":"spn-113150","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-113151","marks":["code"],"text":"reopen_after_closure"},{"id":"spn-113152","text":" are DELETED: finality"}]}],"id":"blk-58578","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58580","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113153","text":"now materializes the successor vacancy atomically with the admission advance, so no second mint path for a vacancy exists, and the warden's "},{"id":"spn-113154","marks":["code"],"text":"min_generation"},{"id":"spn-113155","text":" fence became unnecessary. <!-- /historical -->"}]},{"id":"blk-58581","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58583","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113156","marks":["code"],"text":"suspend"},{"id":"spn-113157","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-113158","marks":["code"],"text":"recover_attachment"},{"id":"spn-113159","text":" do not change lifecycle state; recovery"}]}],"id":"blk-58582","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58584","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113160","text":"is judged against "},{"id":"spn-113161","marks":["code"],"text":"&Admission"},{"id":"spn-113162","text":" (borrowed) exactly as in R0.4.6."}]},{"id":"blk-58585","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58587","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113163","text":"Public "},{"id":"spn-113164","marks":["code"],"text":"replay_lifecycle"},{"id":"spn-113165","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-113166","marks":["code"],"text":"audit_replay"},{"id":"spn-113167","text":" over slices remain"}]}],"id":"blk-58586","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58588","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113168","text":"descriptive; a "},{"id":"spn-113169","marks":["code"],"text":"LifecycleState"},{"id":"spn-113170","text":" cannot be passed where an admission is required (type error)."}]},{"id":"blk-58589","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113171","text":"Operational fencing (form 3)"}]},{"id":"blk-58590","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113172","text":"A stale "},{"id":"spn-113173","marks":["code"],"text":"LocusAttachment"},{"id":"spn-113174","text":" may remain representable, but every mutation requires the current admission, which now records Attached(B,1) or Vacant(1): the stale value's "},{"id":"spn-113175","marks":["code"],"text":"detach"},{"id":"spn-113176","text":" fails ("},{"id":"spn-113177","marks":["code"],"text":"WrongGeneration"},{"id":"spn-113178","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-113179","marks":["code"],"text":"WrongCarrier"},{"id":"spn-113180","text":") and hands the stale value back, powerless; its "},{"id":"spn-113181","marks":["code"],"text":"suspend()"},{"id":"spn-113182","text":" custody cannot recover ("},{"id":"spn-113183","marks":["code"],"text":"CustodyMismatch"},{"id":"spn-113184","text":"). stale capability + no current admission = powerless."}]},{"id":"blk-58591","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113185","text":"Who holds the admission"}]},{"id":"blk-58592","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113186","text":"The admission is the controller-side serialization point; carriers hold capability values. Orderly attach/detach need the carrier's value AND the admission; finality needs the warden AND the admission and no carrier cooperation — so a physically lost carrier (its attachment value gone) can still be finalized by the admission holder. Admission hand-off between parties is an explicit move in the one-process model."}]},{"id":"blk-58593","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113187","text":"Boundary (unchanged)"}]},{"id":"blk-58594","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113188","text":"One-process safe-Rust model. No consensus/leases; no durable crash recovery (a persisted admission is bytes); trusted-root lineage forks remain outside the claim (Locus-birth uniqueness is World-level)."}]},{"id":"blk-58595","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113189","text":"Falsifiers (the review's eight)"}]},{"id":"blk-58596","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58598","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113190","text":"detach-then-competing-finality cannot yield two usable vacancies."}]}],"id":"blk-58597","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58600","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113191","text":"consuming a vacancy to attach B leaves no path to a C at that"}]}],"id":"blk-58599","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-58601","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113192","text":"generation, with no separate persistence step involved."}]},{"id":"blk-58602","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58604","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113193","text":"post-finality stale Attachment(A,N) cannot detach or create a successor."}]}],"id":"blk-58603","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58606","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113194","text":"stale vacancy/attachment values without the admission cannot mutate"}]}],"id":"blk-58605","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-58607","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113195","text":"(runtime + type-level: no admission-free transition exists)."}]},{"id":"blk-58608","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58610","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113196","text":"one admission admits exactly one mutation (reuse → E0382)."}]}],"id":"blk-58609","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58612","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113197","text":"failure paths return linear state; retry succeeds without duplicates."}]}],"id":"blk-58611","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58614","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113198","text":"all R0.4.1–R0.4.6 falsifiers remain green."}]}],"id":"blk-58613","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58616","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113199","text":"replay is descriptive; a "},{"id":"spn-113200","marks":["code"],"text":"LifecycleState"},{"id":"spn-113201","text":" is not an admission."}]}],"id":"blk-58615","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierap2blend3ztmmkajzy7xukepmbxqxt2jso7c34fu72sti5r5tgjba","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}